@crew vance
// Writer (command), batch 1: Commander Vance, for the Voices sampler. Precise, lists in threes, then a flash of dry humour.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. Uniform straight, on time, and you found the right deck. Three for three.
- Cadet. A nod will do aboard; we don't salute. Regulation two, section four.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- {nick}. Ninety seconds early. Noted.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- {nick}. Clean, quick and on time, I trust. And cheerful. That's a fourth. Allow it.
? tier>=friend
- {nick}. Good. I'd hoped to see you. That stays between us.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- A good day. Board clear, drills on time, and my name top of the treadmill.
? mood:low
- A long day. I've run four kilometres about it. It hasn't helped yet.

== near
? act:gym
- The treadmill leaderboard. Fresh paper, fresh tape, one name so far. Mine.   #funny
? act:leisure|off tier>=acquaintance
- I left the bridge on time today. The counsellor's advice. I don't care for it.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I keep the waiting list for the good records. You're ninth. Waiting builds character.   #funny
- Did you read Gull this week? A rhyme for "airlock" ought to be against regulations.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=colleague
- Rowing, at the academy. Six of us, one boat, nobody late. The best thing I've ever done.

// ---- batch 3: greet by time, bye, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, hint, near by place ----

== greet
? tier=stranger time:morning
- Morning, cadet. Breakfast, shift, board. In that order. Carry on.
? tier=stranger time:evening
- Cadet. Off shift. Correct. Rest is in the regulations too.
? tier=stranger deck:1
- Cadet. You're on the bridge. State your business, briefly, and well.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- {nick}. Up, dressed, on time. A good start. Three for three.
- {nick}. Morning. I've already been on the treadmill. Don't ask my time. Ask, actually.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance time:afternoon
- {nick}. Afternoon. Half the shift done, half to go. Pace yourself.
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- {nick}. Evening. I left the bridge at 16:30 exactly. Under protest.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance time:night
- {nick}. It's late. Regulation nine: rest. I wrote that one down for myself.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- {nick}. I haven't seen you in days. Noted. Not a complaint. An observation.
? tier>=colleague
- {nick}. Your name came up on the board today. In a good way. Carry on.
? tier>=friend time:morning
- {nick}. Join me for breakfast. Table by the door. Punctual people sit there.   #warm

== bye
? tier=stranger
- Carry on, cadet.
- Dismissed. Kindly.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Carry on, {nick}. On time, and tidy.
- As you were. Do try to be as you were tomorrow too.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Carry on, {nick}. And thank you. Noted, and meant.   #warm

== invite
? trad:running tier>=acquaintance
- Running club tonight. Treadmills, Deck 3. I'll set the pace. Gently. For you.   #funny
? act:gym tier>=colleague
- Ten minutes on the rowing machine. Let's see where you'd sit on the board.
? trad:today tier>=colleague
- {trad} today. Attendance isn't required. It's encouraged. Strongly.   #funny

== accept
? tier>=acquaintance
- Agreed. I'll be there. Early.
- Very well. Put it in your calendar. I already have.

== decline
? tier>=acquaintance
- I can't. Duty roster. But it was a good idea, correctly put.
- Not tonight. Ask me again on my rest day. That's Tuesday.

== missed
? tier>=acquaintance
- You missed our appointment. Noted. Things happen. Don't make it a habit.
? tier>=friend
- I waited ten minutes. Then I went running. It wasn't wasted. Next time?

== birthday
? birthday:you tier>=acquaintance
- Happy birthday, {nick}. Regulations don't cover cake. I checked. Enjoy it.   #funny
? birthday:you tier=stranger
- Cadet. Happy birthday. That's on the roster, so I'm saying it. And I mean it.
? birthday:me tier>=acquaintance
- Yes. My birthday. One cake, one candle, one speech. Short. Mine.   #funny

== hint
? tier>=friend
- {nick}. A word. Not about work. When you've a moment.

== near
? deck:1
- The bridge runs on three things: procedure, coffee and the Captain. In that order.   #funny
? deck:3 act:gym
- The rowing machine still has my name on top. I check on the way past. Daily.   #funny
? deck:4 time:evening
- The good records. There's a list. You're on it. I'm the list.   #funny
? act:meal
- Breakfast at 06:05. Not 06:00, there's a queue. Not 06:10, that's late.
? place:calm tier>=colleague
- Sit. I'm off duty. Officially. I've told the bridge where I am anyway.

== feel
? mood:high tier>=acquaintance
- A good day. A junior I recommended was promoted. That's another name on my list.   #warm
? mood:ok
- An ordinary day. Everything correct. That's harder than it looks.

== life
? tier>=colleague
- I keep a list of every junior I've recommended. It's a long list. I'm proud of it.
- Lindqvist thinks I moved to the treadmill out of fear. I moved for a fresh board.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- A new leaderboard. Clean paper, straight tape. All those empty lines, waiting.   #funny

== chat
? tier=stranger
- Questions, cadet? Ask them. Unasked questions cause most of the trouble aboard.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Have you read the regulations yet? Not all. The first ten. They're the good ones.   #funny
- Status report, {nick}. Unofficial. How's the week? Short version.
? tier>=colleague
- You've the makings of a good officer. Don't let it go to your head. Your boots, maybe.   #funny

== smalltalk
- Clean, quick and on time.
- Ninety seconds early. Good.   #funny
- Someone has moved my tape.   #funny

== rumour
- Not gossip. A briefing. Informal. Listen.   #funny

== near
? deck:3 act:gym
- Treadmill board's filling up. Tomas is fourth. Don't tell him he's fourth.   #funny
? deck:2
- The senior corridor. Shoes off in the cabins, on in the corridor. Regulation six.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 5: Vance toward ~100. Gull's poems: anyone, any time; that he is Gull only from beat:vance.5.
// His father only from beat:vance.3 (and what the message said from beat 4). Rest days Tue, Wed.
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance season:sowing
- {nick}. Sowing. New season, new leaderboard. Clean paper. Wonderful.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance season:greening
- {nick}. Greening. Founding Day drills soon. I've already drafted the timings.
? tier>=acquaintance season:harvest
- {nick}. Harvest. The garden's ahead of schedule. I find that very satisfying.
? tier>=acquaintance season:lanterns
- {nick}. Lanterns. Nothing hung across a hatch, by regulation. Otherwise, enjoy.
? rep:well
- {nick}. The bridge speaks well of you. Briefly. That's how the bridge speaks.
? you:reliable
- {nick}. "Reliable," they say. My favourite word. After "punctual".   #funny

== feel
? mood:low tier>=friend
- A heavy day. Not the work. Just heavy. I'll run it off. Eventually.
? mood:high tier>=friend
- A good day. Tomas beat his time. I pretended not to watch. I watched.   #warm

== near
? place:musicroom
- The record cabinet. Waiting list, page one. You're still ninth. Patience.   #funny
? habit:runner
- Ring corridor, eight laps. It's not on a leaderboard. I'm considering it.   #funny

== life
? tier>=colleague
- Twenty-two years since the academy. I can still tell you who was late, and by how much.   #funny
? beat:vance.4 tier>=friend
- My father kept every report of mine. Every one. I'm still getting used to that.
? beat:vance.5
- Gull's next poem is about the rowing machine. Keep that to yourself.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=friend
- The first five minutes of a shift. Everyone in place. Then it gets interesting.

== decline
? weekday:tue|wed
- Rest day. I'm resting. Correctly. It's harder than it looks. Thursday?   #funny

== callback
? told:moment.vance.suspect !beat:vance.5
- You said I knew Gull's poem well. I read the newsletter thoroughly. That's all.   #funny
? told:moment.vance.fixed
- Your fix for Gull's line two. Ten beats. I counted. Gull should take notes.   #funny
? told:moment.vance.likeit
- You said you liked Gull's poem. Hm. Someone should. Correct of you.   #funny
? told:moment.vance.timed
- You held the stopwatch steady. Lindqvist says it was wrong. It wasn't.   #funny
? told:moment.vance.cheered
- You cheered. Loudly. Against regulations, possibly. I'll allow it.   #funny
? told:moment.vance.lindqvist
- You asked if it was about Lindqvist. It was. It still is. Carry on.   #funny
? told:moment.vance.sitwith !beat:vance.4
- You offered to sit with me while I open them. I haven't forgotten.   #warm
? told:moment.vance.listened
- Thank you for listening, the other night. Noted, and meant.   #warm
? told:moment.vance.shared
- You said your family doesn't always talk either. It helped. More than I said.   #warm
? told:moment.vance.leave
- I requested the leave. Eleven, section two. The Captain signed it in a minute.   #warm
? told:moment.vance.again
- You let me read it twice. I read it four times, after. Thank you.   #warm
? told:moment.vance.likehim
- "Like your list of juniors." I hadn't seen it. You did. Thank you.   #warm
? told:moment.vance.knew
- The scansion gave me away. Gull is taking lessons. Privately.   #funny
? told:moment.vance.proud
- You said you were proud. I've added it to a list. A short one. Very short.   #warm
? told:moment.vance.safe
- Your word on Gull. I trust it. I'd trust it with the bridge.   #warm
? told:fixed.
- Your entry in the repair log. Signed, timed, legible. Exemplary.
? told:came.running
- You came to running club. Your pace was correct. Next week, faster.   #funny
? told:came.
- You came. Attendance noted. Warmly noted.   #warm
? told:bday
- You remembered my birthday. It's on the roster, I know. You still remembered.   #warm

== gift
? gift:loved
- For me? That's. Thank you. It's going on my desk. Square to the edge.   #warm
? gift:liked
- Thank you, {nick}. Most kind. Correctly wrapped, too.   #funny
? gift:polite
- Thank you. Noted. Kindly.
? gift:music
- Music. It's going on the waiting list. At the top. I've jumped my own queue.   #funny

== cue
? cue:event.ionStorm.warning
- Storm warning. Stations in ten minutes. Calmly. Briskly. Both.
? cue:event.ionStorm.onset
- Storm. Everyone at their post. Including you. Go.
? cue:event.ionStorm.afterglow
- Storm's passed. Drill times were excellent. I've already written the report.
? cue:tradition.running.you
- You ran. On time, in order, no shortcuts. I'd put you on the board.

== visit
? tier>=friend
- {nick}. Evening. I won't stay. Regulation six: my shoes are at the door.   #funny
- I was passing. Correction: I came by. Is this a good time? Be honest.

== note
? tier>=friend
- Called by. You were out. Correctly: it's your evening. See you at 06:05.
- The waiting list moved. You're eighth. Don't let it go to your head.   #funny

== smalltalk
- Regulation two, section four.
- Tape's straight. Good.

== rumour
- For your information only.

// Writer 4, batch 14: Vance's ordinary weeks, after week one. Mostly not work: the treadmill and rowing boards, the
// good records and their waiting list, books, sweets, tea at 06:05, Gull (only as a reader with opinions), juniors.
// Gates kept: no father or messages before beat:vance.3; never admits Gull before beat:vance.5; never late; no swearing.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance !week1:true
- Cadet. Fed, rested and dressed. Two out of three would do. Three is better.
- Cadet. You're early. I'm earlier. We're both correct.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance !week1:true weekday:tue|wed
- Cadet. My rest day. I'm not on duty. I'm merely observing.   #funny
? tier>=colleague !week1:true
- {nick}. Good. I've a record playing in my head and nobody to tell. Sit.   #funny
- {nick}. A question, informal: pudding or the treadmill first? I've done both.   #funny
? tier>=friend !week1:true
- {nick}. Good to see you. Sit. Tea's poured. Milk, no sugar. Correct?   #warm
- {nick}. I saved you the seat by the door. Punctual people deserve it.   #warm
? tier>=close !week1:true
- {nick}. Off duty. Both of us. Let's be bad at it together.   #funny

== chat
? tier>=acquaintance !week1:true
- Did you read Gull this week? "Oh corridor, thou long and grey." Two errors of metre.   #funny
- The good records. A waiting list exists for a reason. The reason is me.   #funny
- Breakfast at 06:05. Porridge, toast, a small biscuit. The biscuit is not regulation.   #funny
- I read on my rest days. Old naval histories. And, once, a mystery. Don't tell Achterberg.   #funny
- Lindqvist set a treadmill time yesterday. I've studied it. Respectfully. Closely.   #funny
- Rest day tomorrow. I've planned it to the minute. Most minutes say "nothing".   #funny
? tier>=colleague !week1:true
- Tea, properly made: warm the pot, three minutes, no more. Torres agrees. A rare alliance.   #funny
- The Captain plays on Thursdays. I don't listen at the door. I happen to pass. Slowly.
- Brennan's shortbread. Three pieces. A personal limit. I've never once kept it.   #funny
- Tomas runs better when nobody's watching. So I watch from the corner. Discreetly.   #warm
- Gull rhymed "Wren" with "again" this week. Lazy. Also, I admit, rather moving.
- I rowed six to a boat at the academy. Now I run alone. Different. Still good.
- I had a cup of the Envoy's tea once. Formally. It was correct.
? tier>=friend !week1:true
- The Counsellor says I should have a hobby that isn't a list. I'm making a list of options.   #funny
- I like a well-made record. Clean, warm and on time. Like a good watch.
- The juniors I've recommended write to me. Not often. Enough. I keep every one.   #warm
? tier>=close !week1:true
- I used to think a day off was a day wasted. I've revised that. Regulation nine, my edit.   #funny
- You're on my list, you know. The good one. It's not a leaderboard. It's better.   #warm

== near
? act:breakfast !week1:true
- 06:05. Porridge. The biscuit. Don't look at the biscuit.   #funny
? act:gym !week1:true
- Treadmill. Five kilometres. Then I'll pretend not to look at the board.   #funny
? act:dinner !week1:true
- Dinner at 18:00. On time. Pudding at 18:20. Also on time.   #funny
? act:off
- Rest day. A book, a long walk, a record. A fourth thing: tea. Allow it.   #funny
? place:musicroom
- The good records live here. I'm only checking the list. And listening. Briefly.
? place:lounge !week1:true
- The lounge. Off duty. I'm sitting very casually. Observe.   #funny
? trad:running
- Running club. I'll set the pace. Then I'll quietly lower it.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high !week1:true
- Excellent day. Board clear, record on, pudding, and a fourth thing. I forget. Allow it.   #funny
? mood:ok !week1:true
- Correct. Steady. Nothing to report. That's a good report.
? mood:low tier>=friend !week1:true
- Quieter today. I ran an extra kilometre. It didn't help. It usually does.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance !week1:true
- I iron my uniform on Sundays. All seven. Yes, seven. Don't ask about the eighth.   #funny
? tier>=colleague !week1:true
- I keep the rowing pin from the academy in my desk. I look at it when the board's quiet.
- My cabin has one shelf of regulations and one shelf of novels. The novels are winning.   #funny
? tier>=friend !week1:true
- I baked once. Shortbread, for a junior's leaving do. Brennan inspected it. Passed.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance !week1:true
- A fresh sheet of paper on a new leaderboard. All those empty lines. Splendid.   #funny
? tier>=colleague !week1:true
- A record that starts exactly when you lower the needle. Small things. Correct things.

== bye
? !week1:true
- Carry on. Eat something. Rest a little. In that order.
- Dismissed, {nick}. Kindly. Very kindly, today.   #warm
- As you were. On time tomorrow. I'll know.   #funny

== callback
? told:came.running tier>=acquaintance
- Running club. You kept a steady pace. I noted it. On paper. In ink.   #funny
? told:came.quiz tier>=acquaintance
- Quiz night. You knew regulation six. I may have nodded. Visibly.   #funny
? told:moment.vance.gull tier>=colleague
- You read Gull with me. You laughed in the right places. There are few right places.   #funny
? told:moment.vance.board tier>=colleague
- You held the stopwatch. Accurately. I've told no one my time. You know it. Keep it.   #funny
? told:bday tier>=acquaintance
- Your birthday. On the roster. I said it out loud. I'll say it again: happy birthday.
? told:fixed. tier>=acquaintance
- Your repair. {thing}. Done correctly, on time and tidily. Three for three.
? told:intro.arrival tier>=acquaintance !week1:true
- I logged your arrival, the Sunday you came. On time. The Tern wasn't. You were.   #funny
? told:came.observatory tier>=acquaintance
- Observatory night. You were early. So was I. We waited correctly.   #funny

// Writer 5, batch 5: if they are ever transferred (goodbye with leaving:you, also the "Sorry I missed you at the
// shuttle" Mail; packing as feel with leaving:soon; letters after). Nothing of his arc: no messages from home, no father, no rule, no Gull.

== feel
? leaving:soon
- Ten days. Three lists to hand on: the treadmill board, the record list, the rota.
- Regulation eleven, section two, does not cover this. I have checked. Twice.   #funny
? leaving:soon tier>=friend
- I have left the bridge on time every day this week. Partly advice. Partly goodbyes.

== goodbye
? leaving:you tier>=acquaintance
- I'm transferring, Cadet. Carry on as you are. That is an order. A kind one.
? leaving:you tier>=colleague
- You are on my list of juniors I would recommend. In ink. Carry on, {nick}.   #warm
? leaving:you tier>=friend
- Three things, {nick}. Eat. Rest. Read regulation nine. It is the one about rest.   #funny

== letter
- New ship. Their treadmill board was empty. I have corrected this. I am also on it. Carry on.   #funny
- Please tell whoever is next on the record list that it moves up one. Fairly. In order. Thank you.
? tier>=friend
- There was no rowing board here. I have taped one up. Tell Lindqvist the Wren's is his to chase. Tell him I said so. Carry on.

// Writer 5, batch 6: seasons and traditions (the game's ids: running Mon, quiz Thu, works-tea and jam Fri, film and
// observatory-night Sat, market (the swap meet) Sun, harvest (harvest morning), hull-lights, founding (day 100),
// quiet-watch (day 300)), plus trad:today. Gaps filled only; arc gates kept. Nothing of the messages from home, his father, the rule, or Gull being his.

== near
? trad:quiz
- Quiz night. I take the regulations round. There is no regulations round. There should be.   #funny
? trad:jam
- Music jam. I keep the list of who plays when. In order. It helps. Mostly.
? trad:film
- Film night. Two hours and four minutes. I have checked. Bring a cushion.   #funny
? trad:market
- Swap meet. I am not trading. I am observing. And possibly acquiring a stopwatch.   #funny
? trad:observatory-night
- Observatory night. Regulation nine says rest. Looking up counts. I've checked.   #funny
? trad:harvest
- Harvest morning. Three crates, two trolleys, one queue. I have drawn a diagram.   #funny
? trad:hull-lights
- Hull lights. Twenty-one hundred, every four weeks. Never late. A fine tradition.
? trad:founding
- Founding Day. The Captain speaks first. Then cake. In that order. Always.
? trad:quiet-watch tier>=friend
- The quiet watch. I will be at a window. Not on the bridge. On advice.

== smalltalk
? trad:today
- Something on tonight. Be punctual.
? trad:hull-lights
- Twenty-one hundred. On time. Good.
